{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-32706" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $x={y}^{5}+3y-5,$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at the point $(33,2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032433/state.json" "file_sha256" "30b785885a02712960713b86e8ba80925d27f4358c997f38028ec6ce0308bdf7"} {"question" "q-32706" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{5}+3y-5) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{5})+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y)-5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(1) \\\\  & =5{y}^{4}+3(1)+0 \\\\  & =5{y}^{4}+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{5{y}^{4}+3}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the point $(33,2),$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(33,2)} & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot {2}^{4}+3}=\\frac{1}{83}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032433/state.json" "file_sha256" "30b785885a02712960713b86e8ba80925d27f4358c997f38028ec6ce0308bdf7"} {"question" "q-32706" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032433/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c5efd0a965a3293c70a0a5370c37421bfa4db8a96f8c88b157e904508ad8bf57"} {"question" "q-32706" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032433/state.json" "file_sha256" "30b785885a02712960713b86e8ba80925d27f4358c997f38028ec6ce0308bdf7"} {"question" "q-32706" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "43"] ["math" "83"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{29}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{43}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{83}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032433/state.json" "file_sha256" "30b785885a02712960713b86e8ba80925d27f4358c997f38028ec6ce0308bdf7"} {"question" "q-32706" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{83}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032433/state.json" "file_sha256" "30b785885a02712960713b86e8ba80925d27f4358c997f38028ec6ce0308bdf7"} {"question" "q-170188" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given a curve $x=5{y}^{5}-3{y}^{3},$ what is the equation of the tangent to the curve at the point $(-2,-1)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032433/state.json" "file_sha256" "30b785885a02712960713b86e8ba80925d27f4358c997f38028ec6ce0308bdf7"} {"question" "q-170188" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(5{y}^{5}-3{y}^{3}) \\\\  & =5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{5})-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{3}) \\\\  & =5\\cdot (5{y}^{4})-3\\cdot (3{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =25{y}^{4}-9{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{25{y}^{4}-9{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $(-2,-1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(-2,-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25(-1)^{4}-9(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point-slope formula for a tangent line, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-1) & =\\frac{1}{16}(x-(-2)) \\\\ y+1 & =\\frac{1}{16}(x+2) \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{16}+\\frac{2}{16}-1 \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{16}+\\frac{1}{8}-1 \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{16}-\\frac{7}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032433/state.json" "file_sha256" "30b785885a02712960713b86e8ba80925d27f4358c997f38028ec6ce0308bdf7"} {"question" "q-170188" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032433/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c5efd0a965a3293c70a0a5370c37421bfa4db8a96f8c88b157e904508ad8bf57"} {"question" "q-170188" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032433/state.json" "file_sha256" "30b785885a02712960713b86e8ba80925d27f4358c997f38028ec6ce0308bdf7"} {"question" "q-170188" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=16x+31"] ["math" "y=16x-14"] ["math" "y=\\frac{x}{16}+\\frac{9}{8}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{x}{16}-\\frac{15}{16}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{x}{16}-\\frac{7}{8}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032433/state.json" "file_sha256" "30b785885a02712960713b86e8ba80925d27f4358c997f38028ec6ce0308bdf7"} {"question" "q-170188" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{x}{16}-\\frac{7}{8}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032433/state.json" "file_sha256" "30b785885a02712960713b86e8ba80925d27f4358c997f38028ec6ce0308bdf7"} {"question" "q-312553" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given a curve $x=3y-{y}^{2},$ what is the equation of the tangent to the curve at the point $(0,3)?$\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032433/state.json" "file_sha256" "30b785885a02712960713b86e8ba80925d27f4358c997f38028ec6ce0308bdf7"} {"question" "q-312553" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(3y-{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =3(1)-2y \\\\  & =3-2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{3-2y}.\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $(0,3)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(0,3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3-2(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-3)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point-slope formula for a tangent line, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-3 & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (x-0) \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{3}x+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032433/state.json" "file_sha256" "30b785885a02712960713b86e8ba80925d27f4358c997f38028ec6ce0308bdf7"} {"question" "q-312553" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032433/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c5efd0a965a3293c70a0a5370c37421bfa4db8a96f8c88b157e904508ad8bf57"} {"question" "q-312553" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032433/state.json" "file_sha256" "30b785885a02712960713b86e8ba80925d27f4358c997f38028ec6ce0308bdf7"} {"question" "q-312553" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{x}{3}+3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032433/state.json" "file_sha256" "30b785885a02712960713b86e8ba80925d27f4358c997f38028ec6ce0308bdf7"} {"question" "q-341634" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $x=4{y}^{4}-3y,$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at the point $(1,1).$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(1,1)}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032433/state.json" "file_sha256" "30b785885a02712960713b86e8ba80925d27f4358c997f38028ec6ce0308bdf7"} {"question" "q-341634" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(4{y}^{4}-3y) \\\\  & =4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{4})-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y) \\\\  & =4(4{y}^{3})-3 \\\\  & =16{y}^{3}-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{16{y}^{3}-3}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the point $(1,1),$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(1,1)} & =\\frac{1}{16({1}^{3})-3}=\\frac{1}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032433/state.json" "file_sha256" "30b785885a02712960713b86e8ba80925d27f4358c997f38028ec6ce0308bdf7"} {"question" "q-341634" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032433/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c5efd0a965a3293c70a0a5370c37421bfa4db8a96f8c88b157e904508ad8bf57"} {"question" "q-341634" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032433/state.json" "file_sha256" "30b785885a02712960713b86e8ba80925d27f4358c997f38028ec6ce0308bdf7"} {"question" "q-341634" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{13}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032433/state.json" "file_sha256" "30b785885a02712960713b86e8ba80925d27f4358c997f38028ec6ce0308bdf7"} {"question" "q-341751" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $x=-\\frac{16}{\\sqrt[3]{y}}+13,$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at the point $(5,8).$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(5,8)}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032433/state.json" "file_sha256" "30b785885a02712960713b86e8ba80925d27f4358c997f38028ec6ce0308bdf7"} {"question" "q-341751" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-\\frac{16}{\\sqrt[3]{y}}+13) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-16{y}^{-1/3}+13) \\\\  & =-16\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-1/3})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(13) \\\\  & =-16(-\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{-4/3})+0 \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}{y}^{-4/3} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3{(\\sqrt[3]{y})}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{3{(\\sqrt[3]{y})}^{4}}{16}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the point $(5,8),$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(5,8)} & =\\frac{3{(\\sqrt[3]{8})}^{4}}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(16)}{16} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032433/state.json" "file_sha256" "30b785885a02712960713b86e8ba80925d27f4358c997f38028ec6ce0308bdf7"} {"question" "q-341751" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032433/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c5efd0a965a3293c70a0a5370c37421bfa4db8a96f8c88b157e904508ad8bf57"} {"question" "q-341751" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032433/state.json" "file_sha256" "30b785885a02712960713b86e8ba80925d27f4358c997f38028ec6ce0308bdf7"} {"question" "q-341751" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032433/state.json" "file_sha256" "30b785885a02712960713b86e8ba80925d27f4358c997f38028ec6ce0308bdf7"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1222 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
